{
  "id": "u01",
  "section": 1,
  "title": "Hello",
  "tip": {
    "en": "The verb olla (to be) changes with the person: minä olen, sinä olet, hän on, me olemme, te olette, he ovat. Hän means both he and she.\n\nVowel harmony: the vowels a, o, u do not mix with ä, ö, y inside one word. The vowels e and i go with both groups. Endings follow the word: talo + ssa, metsä + ssä."
  },
